# service_gap_cmdbuf_scattered: Command buffers that cross a page boundary where the next page is elsewhere: VA pages 4, 5 and 6 are a first-range page, a page of a second RAM range, and a first-range page far from the first. Each command buffer (one blit segment of three fills, the middle record straddling the boundary) is read as two pieces: the service's cursor starts a new range where the host addresses stop being adjacent, in-process the copy walks page by page. A third command buffer crosses physically adjacent pages and is one piece. Every fill lands in every setup.
